    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.git\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.12 (!at least latest Nightly build!)\n\n### Description\n\nDisclamer: I assume the issue is with how mini-git creates a buffer, because the shown behavior isn't reproduced for e.g. `neogit`\n\nIssue: whenever I try to accept suggestion provided by cmp (blink in my example) the suggestion is applied to the previous buffer and gitcommit buffer is closed.\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/19d29682-da86-4114-a306-37f81e5a5206",
